---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import QuickAnswer from '../components/QuickAnswer.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import BreadcrumbSchema from '../components/schema/BreadcrumbSchema.astro';
import PersonSchema from '../components/schema/PersonSchema.astro';
import FAQPageSchema from '../components/schema/FAQPageSchema.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

const pressFaqs = [
  {
    q: 'What is Pour Picks?',
    a: 'Pour Picks is an iPhone app for adult bourbon collectors. The AI reads a bottle\'s label and adds it to your cellar, a short quiz called Bourbon DNA learns your palate and names the bottle to buy next, and Pour Tonight picks a bottle to open from what you already own. It\'s free to download, and Cask Club ($5.99 a month or $49.99 a year) removes the free limits and adds more features.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Who is the founder of Pour Picks?',
    a: 'I am. I\'m Bob Guillow, and I built Pour Picks on my own. It\'s published by Timberline Ventures LLC, my single-member LLC, with no outside investment and no parent company.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What makes Pour Picks different from other whiskey apps?',
    a: 'Pour Picks is built around your own cellar and your palate. Pour Tonight picks from bottles you already own, Bourbon DNA names the bottle to buy next and why, and the label scanner lets you correct a match before it\'s saved. The app has no ads or purchase links, and I don\'t sell user data.',
  },
];

const quickAnswer =
  'Pour Picks is an iPhone app for bourbon collectors that I built on my own. ' +
  'It launched on the App Store on May 9, 2026. ' +
  'Brand assets and screenshots are available on request at ' + SITE.supportEmail + '.';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Press"
  description="The Pour Picks fact sheet and boilerplate, and how to reach me for brand assets or a review copy."
  path="/press"
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <PersonSchema />
    <FAQPageSchema faqs={pressFaqs} />
    <BreadcrumbSchema crumbs={[{ name: 'Press', url: `${SITE.url}/press` }]} />
  </Fragment>

  <p class="brand">{SITE.name}</p>
  <h1>Press Kit</h1>

  <QuickAnswer text={quickAnswer} />

  <p class="press-oneliner">
    Pour Picks is an iPhone app for bourbon collectors. Scan a label and the
    AI adds the bottle to your cellar, then the app keeps track of what you
    own, what you've poured and what it's worth.
  </p>

  <h2>Fact sheet</h2>
  <dl class="factsheet">
    <div class="fact-row"><dt>Product</dt><dd>Pour Picks</dd></div>
    <div class="fact-row"><dt>Tagline</dt><dd>{SITE.tagline}</dd></div>
    <div class="fact-row"><dt>Category</dt><dd>Bourbon and American whiskey cellar app (iOS, free with optional subscription)</dd></div>
    <div class="fact-row"><dt>Platform</dt><dd>iPhone. iPad and Android are not on the near-term roadmap.</dd></div>
    <div class="fact-row"><dt>Launched</dt><dd>May 9, 2026 on the App Store</dd></div>
    <div class="fact-row"><dt>Team</dt><dd>Built and run by one person, Bob Guillow.</dd></div>
    <div class="fact-row"><dt>Funding</dt><dd>Bootstrapped, with no outside investment or advertising partners. Published by Timberline Ventures LLC.</dd></div>
    <div class="fact-row"><dt>Business model</dt><dd>Free to download. Cask Club is $5.99 a month or $49.99 a year, billed through Apple.</dd></div>
    <div class="fact-row"><dt>Catalog</dt><dd>American whiskey: bourbon, rye, Tennessee, wheat and American single malt. It grows as scans turn up corrections and new bottles.</dd></div>
    <div class="fact-row"><dt>Key features</dt><dd>Bourbon DNA, a short palate quiz that names the bottle to buy next and why. Pour Tonight, which picks a bottle to open from the user's own cellar.</dd></div>
    <div class="fact-row"><dt>Not</dt><dd>It isn't a marketplace, retailer or social network. There are no ads or leaderboards.</dd></div>
    <div class="fact-row"><dt>Tech stack</dt><dd>React Native, Expo, Supabase (Postgres with row-level security), Anthropic Claude Vision for the scan engine, Claude for the recommender language.</dd></div>
    <div class="fact-row"><dt>Privacy</dt><dd>No location, health, or financial data collected. Payment information is held by Apple and never touches Pour Picks servers. See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</dd></div>
  </dl>

  <h2>Why I built it</h2>
  <p>
    I kept my collection in a spreadsheet until it got too big to be useful.
    The question I asked most nights was what to pour from what I already
    owned, and the spreadsheet couldn't answer it.
  </p>
  <p>
    So the cellar is the center of the app. Pour Tonight works from your
    shelf, and Bourbon DNA learns your palate before it suggests anything new.
  </p>

  <h2>Boilerplate, paste-ready</h2>

  <div class="pressblock">
    <span class="pressblock-label">Short &middot; ~30 words</span>
    <p>Pour Picks is an iPhone app for bourbon collectors. It scans bottle
    labels into a private cellar, learns your palate, and picks what to pour
    from what you already own. It launched in May 2026.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="pressblock">
    <span class="pressblock-label">Medium &middot; ~60 words</span>
    <p>Pour Picks is an iPhone app for adult bourbon collectors, built by
    solo developer Bob Guillow. The AI reads a bottle's label and adds it to
    your cellar. Bourbon DNA, a short palate quiz, names the bottle to buy
    next and why, and Pour Tonight picks one to open from your own shelf.
    The app is free, with an optional Cask Club membership. It launched on
    the App Store in May 2026.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="pressblock">
    <span class="pressblock-label">Long &middot; ~110 words</span>
    <p>Pour Picks is an iPhone app for adult bourbon collectors, launched on
    the App Store in May 2026 by solo developer Bob Guillow. It reads a
    bottle's label with Claude Vision and adds it to a private cellar, and
    users can correct the match before it's saved. Bourbon DNA, a short
    palate quiz, names the bottle to buy next with the reasons it fits.
    Pour Tonight picks a bottle to open from the user's own shelf, weighted
    to their palate. The catalog covers American whiskey and grows through
    scan corrections. Pour Picks is bootstrapped, sells no data, shows no
    ads and does not sell alcohol. The app is free to download, and Cask
    Club is $5.99 a month or $49.99 a year.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Brand assets</h2>
  <p>
    A high-resolution app icon, App Store screenshots, hero images and a
    founder headshot are available on request. Email
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a> with
    "Press assets" in the subject and I'll send a Drive link, usually the
    same day. The screenshots are also on the
    <a href={SITE.appStoreUrl} rel="noopener">App Store listing</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Reviewer access</h2>
  <p>
    If you're a journalist, podcaster or reviewer and want to spend real
    time with the app, I can give you a year of Cask Club. Email
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>
    with the email tied to your App Store account and I'll set it up,
    usually the same day. There's no expectation of coverage, and honest
    reviews are welcome, good or bad.
  </p>

  <h2>Quick links</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>App Store listing: <a href={SITE.appStoreUrl} rel="noopener">{SITE.appStoreUrl}</a></li>
    <li>Web home: <a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url}</a></li>
    <li>About page (canonical company info): <a href="/about">/about</a></li>
    <li>Articles and editorial: <a href="/articles">/articles</a></li>
    <li>Privacy policy: <a href="/privacy">/privacy</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Press, partnership, podcast and review requests go to
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>.
    I usually reply within a day.
  </p>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
